__pycache__/
*.pyc

# canix_sync.py's own incremental-fetch working state for the two resources
# that actually grow unboundedly (packages: ~6KB/record incl. full COA/test
# panels; transfers: ~12KB/record incl. nested source/destination detail).
# canix_packages_history.json alone hit 137MB, over GitHub's 100MB hard
# limit, the first time it was committed; transfers was already 46.5MB.
# Kept on disk locally; in CI, persisted across runs via actions/cache in
# .github/workflows/canix_sync.yml instead of git.
#
# canix_plant_batches.json and canix_harvests.json are NOT excluded — they
# grow far slower (a season's worth of outdoor batches/harvests, not every
# package tag ever printed) and canix_inventory.html's forecast view reads
# plant_batches directly, so it needs to be git-tracked like
# canix_inventory.json is.
data/canix_packages_history.json
data/canix_transfers.json
